> Q6.) How specifically would you assess the results of this pipeline for accuracy?
>Assessing the accuracy of a SNP calling pipeline comes down to three basic checks. First, you compare the called variants against a known truth set or answer key using an evaluation script to measure precision and recall. Second, check the summary stats from the VCF file since haploids have one set of chromosomes, a real mutation should have nearly 100% read support instead of a 50/50 split, and overall DNA changes should hit a 2.0 ratio. Third, visually inspect variants in a genome browser like IGV to confirm that the sequencing reads line up cleanly across the site without clustering errors near the ends of reads.

